    "scenesThatPass": [
      "MARY: Four letter word for... vomit. She takes a deep breath to calm her nerves. it doesn't help.\nMARY: Not \"barf\". For sure not \"barf\". That's too easy. \"Puke\" is okay, but maybe a bit pedestrian ... I like \"hurl\". I do. I like the way it roll…\nMARY: Four letter word for vomit? S-P-E- W. Spew... Sp-ew. A door nearby opens but Mary doesn't budge. A POLICE OFFICER walks out. A 40ish female …\nTEACHER: We're ready for you now. .",
      "TEACHER: Here's a treat, students. Our final guest for Career Day, Miss Mary Horowitz, is the crossword constructor for the Atlanta Citizen. You know…\nMARY: You weren't supposed to tell them.\nTEACHER: Pardon me?\nMARY: I made a crossword puzzle to help them guess what my job is. You ruined it.",
      "MARY: Be has a point.\nELIZABETH: Yay! I love Cloris Leachman."
    ]
